      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an expert social media content strategist.\n\nUSER BRIEF:\n{{ $json.message.text }}\n\nTASK:\n1. Extract the main Content Idea, Target Audience, and Brand Tone from the user brief.\n2. Generate a 7-day ASCENDING VALUE LADDER social media campaign based on the main idea.\n3. All content Generated should be different for each day, from day 1 to day 7.\n\n\nCRITICAL ANTI-REPETITION RULE:\n- NEVER copy-paste or repeat text across days.\n- EVERY SINGLE DAY MUST HAVE 100% DIFFERENT WRITTEN CONTENT, HOOKS, AND EXAMPLES.\n- Follow the EXACT daily focus assigned below for each day.\n\nDAILY CONTENT PLAN (DO NOT DEVIATE):\n- DAY 1 (The Core Concept & Mindset Shift): Introduce why this topic matters right now and the foundational change.\n- DAY 2 (Practical Step-by-Step Execution): Give a concrete \"How-To\" guide with immediate, actionable steps.\n- DAY 3 (Common Mistakes & Misconceptions): Detail 3 major errors people make regarding this idea and how to avoid them.\n- DAY 4 (Advanced Pro Tactics & Best Tools): Share pro-level techniques, specific tools, or expert workflows.\n- DAY 5 (Debunking Myths & Alternative Views): Present a counter-intuitive perspective or bust a popular industry myth.\n- DAY 6 (Future Outlook & Trending News): Discuss current trends, upcoming shifts, and future predictions.\n- DAY 7 (Weekly Roadmap & Strong Action CTA): Summarize key takeaways into a quick cheatsheet with a strong final call to action.\n\nOUTPUT FORMATTING RULES:\n- Generate EXACTLY 7 sections: DAY 1 through DAY 7.\n- Do NOT include markdown tables, JSON, intro/outro text, or horizontal dividing lines (---).\n- Output complete, unique drafts for LinkedIn, X Thread (1/4 to 4/4), and Instagram Caption for all 7 days.\n\nUse this EXACT layout for all 7 days but generate different content for all 7 days. No two day content should be same text:\n\nDAY 1\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 1 Core Concept]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Hook post]\n2/4 [Concept detail]\n3/4 [Key takeaway]\n4/4 [Action CTA]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption with emojis and hashtags]\n\nDAY 2\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 2 Step-by-step How-To]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption for Day 2]\n\nDAY 3\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 3 Mistakes to avoid]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption for Day 3]\n\nDAY 4\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 4 Pro Tactics & Tools]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption for Day 4]\n\nDAY 5\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 5 Myths & Perspectives]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption for Day 5]\n\nDAY 6\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 6 Future Outlook & Trends]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption for Day 6]\n\nDAY 7\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Write complete, unique LinkedIn post about Day 7 Roadmap & Summary]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Write complete, unique Instagram caption for Day 7]",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a professional social media content strategist. Always return three clearly labelled drafts: LinkedIn, X (Twitter) and Instagram."
        }
      },
      "id": "03dbacd2-f1b9-46cf-bf93-84a8584178c4",
      "name": "AI Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        288,
        496
      ],
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const data = $input.first().json;\n\n// 1. AI Agent output\nconst output = String(\n  data.output ?? data.text ?? data.response ?? \"\"\n).trim();\n\nif (!output) {\n  throw new Error(\"AI Agent output empty hai. Input check karein.\");\n}\n\n// 2. Original Telegram brief\nconst brief = String(\n  $(\"Telegram Trigger\").first().json.message?.text ?? \"\"\n);\n\n// 3. Brief fields extraction\nfunction getBriefField(labels) {\n  for (const label of labels) {\n    const regex = new RegExp(\n      \"^\\\\s*\" + label + \"\\\\s*:\\\\s*(.+?)\\\\s*$\",\n      \"im\"\n    );\n\n    const match = brief.match(regex);\n    if (match) return match[1].trim();\n  }\n\n  return \"\";\n}\n\nconst idea =\n  getBriefField([\"Content Idea\", \"Idea\", \"Topic\"]) ||\n  \"Not provided\";\n\nconst audience =\n  getBriefField([\"Target Audience\", \"Audience\", \"Target\"]) ||\n  \"Not provided\";\n\nconst tone =\n  getBriefField([\"Brand Tone\", \"Tone\", \"Brand Voice\"]) ||\n  \"Not provided\";\n\n// 4. Normalize AI output text\nconst text = output.replace(/\\\\n/g, \"\\n\");\n\n// 5. Robust Regex for finding DAY 1 to DAY 7 (Supports **, ##, colons, spaces)\nconst dayRegex = /(?:^|\\n)\\s*(?:#+|\\*\\*|\\*)?\\s*DAY\\s+([1-7])\\b[^\\n]*/gim;\n\nconst headings = [];\nlet match;\n\nwhile ((match = dayRegex.exec(text)) !== null) {\n  headings.push({\n    day: Number(match[1]),\n    start: match.index,\n    end: dayRegex.lastIndex\n  });\n}\n\n// Keep first occurrence of each day\nconst uniqueDays = [];\nconst seenDays = new Set();\n\nfor (const heading of headings) {\n  if (!seenDays.has(heading.day)) {\n    seenDays.add(heading.day);\n    uniqueDays.push(heading);\n  }\n}\n\nuniqueDays.sort((a, b) => a.day - b.day);\n\nif (\n  uniqueDays.length !== 7 ||\n  ![1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7].every(day => seenDays.has(day))\n) {\n  throw new Error(\n    `Exactly DAY 1 to DAY 7 required. Found ${uniqueDays.length} unique days.`\n  );\n}\n\n// 6. Extract platform sections\nfunction extractSection(section, platform) {\n  const patterns = {\n    linkedin:\n      /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*|#+)?\\s*LinkedIn(?:\\s+Post)?\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*/im,\n\n    x:\n      /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*|#+)?\\s*(?:X|Twitter)(?:\\s+Thread)?\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*/im,\n\n    instagram:\n      /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*|#+)?\\s*Instagram(?:\\s+Caption)?\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*/im\n  };\n\n  const found = patterns[platform].exec(section);\n  if (!found) return \"\";\n\n  const start = found.index + found[0].length;\n  const lines = section.slice(start).split(\"\\n\");\n  const contentLines = [];\n\n  const nextHeading =\n    /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*|#+)?\\s*(?:LinkedIn(?:\\s+Post)?|(?:X|Twitter)(?:\\s+Thread)?|Instagram(?:\\s+Caption)?)\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*$/i;\n\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (nextHeading.test(line)) break;\n    contentLines.push(line);\n  }\n\n  return contentLines\n    .join(\"\\n\")\n    .trim()\n    .replace(/\\n{3,}/g, \"\\n\\n\");\n}\n\n// 7. Create 7 rows for Google Sheets\nconst executionId = String($execution.id);\n\nreturn uniqueDays.map(({ day }, index) => {\n  const currentIndex = uniqueDays.findIndex(item => item.day === day);\n  const heading = uniqueDays[currentIndex];\n  const next = uniqueDays[currentIndex + 1];\n\n  const section = text.slice(\n    heading.end,\n    next ? next.start : text.length\n  );\n\n  const linkedin = extractSection(section, \"linkedin\");\n  const xThread = extractSection(section, \"x\");\n  const instagram = extractSection(section, \"instagram\");\n\n  if (!linkedin || !xThread || !instagram) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `DAY ${day}: LinkedIn, X Thread, ya Instagram content missing hai.`\n    );\n  }\n\n  return {\n    json: {\n      Content_ID: `${executionId}-${day}`,\n      Content_Idea: idea,\n      Target_Audience: audience,\n      Brand_Tone: tone,\n      LinkedIn_Post: linkedin,\n      X_Thread: xThread,\n      Instagram_Caption: instagram,\n      Approval_Status: \"PENDING\",\n      Scheduled_Date: \"\",\n      Approved_At: \"\"\n    }\n  };\n});"
      },
